            "heading": "Key Vocabulary",
            "headingHinglish": "Naye shabd",
            "body": "| Term | Meaning | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Acid** | A chemical substance that turns blue litmus red (and edible, safe acids have a sour taste) | Citric acid in lemons, acetic acid in vinegar, HCl in the lab |\n| **Base** | A chemical substance that turns red litmus blue and neutralises the effect of an acid | Base in soap, baking soda, Ca(OH)₂, NaOH |\n| **Organic acid** | A mild, naturally occurring acid found in plants or animals | Citric acid (lemons), lactic acid (yoghurt/curd), tartaric acid (tamarind/grapes) |\n| **Mineral acid** | A strong laboratory acid prepared from minerals found in the Earth's crust | Hydrochloric acid (HCl), sulphuric acid (H₂SO₄), nitric acid (HNO₃) |\n| **Indicator** | A substance that changes its **colour** or **odour (smell)** to show whether a solution is acidic or basic | Litmus, turmeric, phenolphthalein, methyl orange |\n| **Litmus** | A natural indicator (a purple dye) extracted from lichens (organisms formed by a partnership between a fungus and an alga) | Red in acid, blue in base |\n| **Synthetic indicator** | A human-made indicator synthesised in a laboratory or factory | Phenolphthalein, methyl orange |\n| **Olfactory indicator** | An indicator whose **odour (smell)**—rather than its colour—changes differently in acidic and basic solutions | Onion, vanilla extract, clove oil |",
            "bodyHinglish": "| Shabd | Matlab (simple bhasha mein) | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Acid (aml)** | Wo rasayanik padarth jo neele litmus ko laal kar deta hai (aur khane wale safe acids swaad mein khatte hote hain) | Nimbu mein citric acid, sirke mein acetic acid, lab mein HCl |\n| **Base (kshaarak)** | Wo rasayanik padarth jo laal litmus ko neela kar deta hai aur acid ke asar ko kaatta hai | Sabun mein base, baking soda, Ca(OH)₂, NaOH |\n| **Organic acid** | Paudhon ya jeev-jantuon mein prakritik roop se milne wala halka acid | Citric acid (nimbu), lactic acid (dahi), tartaric acid (imli) |\n| **Mineral acid** | Zameen ke khanijon (minerals) se banaya gaya taakatwar lab acid | Hydrochloric acid (HCl), sulphuric acid (H₂SO₄), nitric acid (HNO₃) |\n| **Indicator (soochak)** | Wo padarth jo apna **rang** ya **gandh (smell)** badal kar batata hai ki ghol acidic hai ya basic | Litmus, haldi (turmeric), phenolphthalein, methyl orange |\n| **Litmus** | Lichen (fungus aur shaival ki saajhedaari se bane chhote jeev) se nikala gaya prakritik indicator (purple rang ka ark) | Acid mein laal, base mein neela |\n| **Synthetic indicator** | Lab ya factory mein banaya gaya manav-nirmit indicator | Phenolphthalein, methyl orange |\n| **Olfactory indicator** | Wo indicator jiska rang nahi, balki **gandh (smell)** acid aur base mein alag hoti hai | Pyaaz (onion), vanilla essence, laung ka tel (clove oil) |"
