            "correctIndex": 3,
            "explanation": "Pitfall to avoid (\"Minerals and ores are the exact same thing.\"): Incorrect. Remember Noah in the museum gallery looking at a chunk of quartz and assuming it was an \"ore.\" Mr. Rivera asked him: \"What metal do we extract from it?\" Quartz contains only silicon and oxygen (SiO₂), with no metal to extract. So quartz is a mineral, not an ore. Similarly, ordinary clay contains aluminium, but extracting it is too expensive, so clay is also a mineral and not an ore. Every ore is a mineral, but not every mineral is an ore.",
