            "explanation": "Pitfall to avoid (\"Cryolite is the ore from which aluminium is extracted.\"): Incorrect: bauxite is the ore of aluminium, and alumina (Al₂O₃) is the compound electrolysed. Look at the electrolysis equation: 2Al₂O₃ → 4Al + 3O₂. Cryolite (Na₃AlF₆) does not get consumed to make the aluminium; it acts as the molten solvent that dissolves alumina at ~950 °C, just as water dissolves salt without being salt itself.",
