            "correctIndex": 3,
            "explanation": "Pitfall to avoid (\"Tin plating and galvanising protect scratched iron in the exact same way.\"): Compare a scratched galvanised bucket and a scratched tin-plated can left out in the rain. Because zinc is more reactive than iron (Zn > Fe), zinc corrodes first at a scratch and protects the iron. Because tin is less reactive than iron (Fe > Sn), the exposed iron corrodes first at a scratch—rusting even faster than bare iron! Both look silvery when new, but behave oppositely once scratched.",
            "explanationHinglish": "Bachke rehna (\"Tin plating bhi galvanising jaisi hi hai.\"): Do khurchi hui cheezein socho: ek galvanised balti aur ek tin-plated dabba. Zinc loha se zyada reactive hai, to khurch par zinc pehle ghulta hai aur loha bachta hai. Tin loha se kam reactive hai, to khurch par loha pehle ghulta hai. Isliye ek saal baad balti theek, dabba khurch ke paas zang se bhara. Dono parat dikhne mein ek jaisi hain, par khurch ke baad kaam ulta hai."
