            "explanation": "Pitfall to avoid (Thinking that electrons flow directly through the liquid electrolyte): *Correction:* Free electrons cannot survive or travel through liquid water or molten salts! Electrons travel strictly through the external metallic wires. Inside the electrolyte, current is carried entirely by physical, migrating cations and anions. At the electrodes, electron transfer occurs like a relay race: the cathode hands electrons to cations, and anions hand electrons back to the anode.",
