            "body": "| Topic | Core Concepts | Unifying Takeaway |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Topic 1** | Electrolytes vs. Non-Electrolytes | Freely mobile ions enable conduction in molten or aqueous states; covalent molecules without ions cannot conduct; strong vs. weak depends on degree of ionisation; metallic conduction (electrons) differs from electrolytic conduction (ions). |\n| **Topic 2** | Mechanism of Electrolysis | Electrolytic cell comprises electrolyte, electrodes, and DC source; Anode is (+), Cathode is (−); Cations $\\rightarrow$ Cathode, Anions $\\rightarrow$ Anode; $\\text{OIL RIG}$ (Oxidation Is Loss at anode, Reduction Is Gain at cathode); molten $\\text{PbBr}_2$ baseline. |\n| **Topic 3** | Selective Discharge | Governed by (1) electrochemical discharge series, (2) ion concentration (brine yields $\\text{Cl}_2$, dilute yields $\\text{O}_2$), and (3) electrode nature (inert vs. active); five fundamental aqueous systems mastered. |\n| **Topic 4** | Electroplating | Target article = Cathode (−); Plating metal = Active Anode (+); Electrolyte = Soluble salt of plating metal; Low steady DC ensures smooth adherent coat; Bath concentration remains constant; Stoichiometry via electron counting. |\n| **Topic 5** | Industrial Applications | Copper refining ($99.99\\%$ purity, anode mud recovery); Chlor-alkali process ($2\\text{NaCl} + 2\\text{H}_2\\text{O} \\rightarrow 2\\text{NaOH} + \\text{Cl}_2 + \\text{H}_2$ in membrane cells); Anodising thickens protective oxide armor on aluminum; Energy economics. |\n| **Topic 6** | Prediction & Synthesis | The Four-Step Algorithm (Inventory $\\rightarrow$ Selection $\\rightarrow$ Half-Equations $\\rightarrow$ Observations); Resolving classic examination puzzles; Mastering multi-concept electrochemical problems. |\n\n---\n\nAs the Science Fair ended, Leo held up his completed scorecard, filled with gold verification stars.\n\nMr. Foster congratulated him: *\"You didn't have to guess or memorize tables blindly. You paused, identified the ions, applied the selection hierarchy, and reasoned out the chemistry.\"*\n\nLeo nodded with a confident smile. *\"No matter what cell or solution is on the bench, the four steps reveal the answer every time!\"*\n\n**What comes next?** In Chapter 5, **\"Mole Concept and Stoichiometry\"** ([mole-concept-and-stoichiometry.md](../mole-concept-and-stoichiometry/mole-concept-and-stoichiometry.md)), we take our quantitative electron accounting to the ultimate level: counting atoms, calculating molar gas volumes, balancing chemical yields, and mastering the universal mathematical language of chemistry!",
            "bodyHinglish": "Ek nazar mein chhe topics ka safar: kaun bijli chalata hai, cell mein kya hota hai, kaun pehle discharge hota hai, plating, refining aur chlor-alkali, aur aakhir mein prediction ka tareeka.\n\n| Topic | Kya seekha | Ek line |\n|---|---|---|\n| Topic 1 | Electrolyte aur non-electrolyte | Free ions ki wajah se pighle ya ghule hue acid, alkali aur salt bijli chalate hain; sugar aur alcohol nahi; strong aur weak electrolyte; metal mein electron, electrolyte mein ions; geele haath aur mains ka khatra. |\n| Topic 2 | Electrolysis kaise hota hai | Cell, anode (+), cathode (−), ions ka chalna, taar mein electron, half-equations, oxidation aur reduction electron ke lene-dene se (OIL RIG), inert aur active electrode, molten PbBr₂, Chapter 3 ke NaCl aur Al₂O₃, do lohe ki keelon ka teacher demo. |\n| Topic 3 | Selective discharge | Jab kai ion hon to order, concentration aur electrode ki kism tay karte hain kaun pehle discharge hoga; paanch mukhya electrolysis (acidified water, concentrated aur dilute NaCl, CuSO₄ inert aur copper electrodes ke saath), summary table, electron gin kar mass, pool chlorinator. |\n| Topic 4 | Electroplating | Cathode par plate hone wali cheez, anode plating dhatu ka, ghol usi dhatu ka salt; ghol ka concentration same rehta hai; silver, nickel, copper plating; strike layer; cyanide aur chromium ki safety; electron ginkar mass; hot-dip galvanising se farq. |\n| Topic 5 | Electrolysis ke aur upyog | Copper ki refining selective discharge se (anode mud), Na, Mg, Al ki extraction, chlor-alkali (Cl₂, H₂, NaOH aur unke upyog), membrane cell, aluminium ki anodising, green hydrogen, bijli ka kharch aur Cl₂ ki safety. |\n| Topic 6 | Predict karo, phir dekho | Chaar kadam ka tareeka (ions, chuno, half-equations, observation), aath puzzle, mixed problems, aam galtiyan aur Chapter ka saar. |\n\n---\n\nStall khatam hone par Tirth ke paas poora ek page bhara tha: chaar kadam, order ki list aur apni teen galtiyan jo ab nahi hongi. Mr. Thatte ne kaha, \"Dekha, ratna nahi pada, bas rukna aur sochna pada: ye ion kahan se aaya, kaun pehle jaayega, electrode kaisa hai.\" Tirth ne sar hilaya, \"Chacha, ab main kisi bhi nayi electrolysis ko dekhkar pehle prediction likhunga, phir dekhunga.\"\n\nTumne Chapter 4 ke saare 6 topics poore kar liye: ab tum jaante ho ki bijli ke saath ions kaise chalte hain, kaun sa ion kahan jaata hai, aur kisi bhi electrolysis ka result pehle se kaise bataya jaata hai.\n\n**Agle Chapter Mein Kya Hai?** Chapter 5 **\"Mole Concept and Stoichiometry\"**: chemists ko ginna bhi aana chahiye: kitne atoms, kitne litre aur kitne gram?"
