            "correctIndex": 3,
            "explanation": "Pitfall to avoid (Dividing percentages directly without dividing by atomic masses first): In Example 1 (80% C, 20% H), if someone simply takes the ratio 80 : 20 = 4 : 1 and writes C₄H, that is completely wrong! 80 : 20 is the ratio of masses, not the ratio of atoms. Because one carbon atom weighs 12 u while one hydrogen atom weighs only 1 u, 80 g of carbon contains far fewer atoms than 20 g of hydrogen. Always divide by atomic masses first: 80 ÷ 12 = 6.67 and 20 ÷ 1 = 20, giving a 1 : 3 atom ratio (CH₃).",
            "explanationHinglish": "Bachke rehna (\"Percent ko sidhe bhaag kar dete hain, atomic mass se nahi.\"): Example 1 mein C = 80%, H = 20%. Agar koi seedha 80 : 20 = 4 : 1 likh de, to formula C₄H nikalega. Ye galat hai: ye mass ka ratio hai, atoms ka nahi. Ek C atom 12 u ka hai aur H sirf 1 u ka, isliye 80 g C mein kam atoms aate hain aur 20 g H mein bahut zyada. Sahi tareeka: 80 ÷ 12 = 6.67 aur 20 ÷ 1 = 20, ratio 1 : 3, yaani CH₃."
