            "body": "Dr. Chen was standing in the bathroom at home with his niece Mia. On the high shelf sat a bottle of heavy-duty toilet bowl cleaner. Mia noticed two hazard symbols printed on the label: one showing a skull and crossbones, and another showing droplets of liquid eating into a hand and a bar of metal. Underneath, in bold letters, it read: \"For adult use only.\"\n\n\"Uncle, what do those symbols mean?\" Mia asked. Without taking the bottle off the shelf, Dr. Chen read the label aloud. \"The first symbol means toxic or seriously harmful. The second means **corrosive**—capable of burning skin, eyes, and metal. It also says: 'Keep out of reach of children' and 'Never mix with bleach or any other household cleaner.'\" \"And what's inside it?\" \"The label names an acid: **hydrochloric acid**. We aren't going to open this bottle, and you should never open it either.\"\n\nMia thought for a moment, then frowned. \"Wait, Uncle—we learned in biology class that our own stomach contains hydrochloric acid! The same chemical that scrubs a toilet bowl is inside me right now? Why doesn't it burn through my stomach?\" Dr. Chen smiled. \"That is a brilliant question. There are two parts to the answer: first, the acid in this bottle is dozens of times more **concentrated** than stomach acid, and second, your stomach wall is lined with a protective coat of mucus. But there's another fascinating twist: what chemists call 'HCl' is both a **gas** and an **aqueous solution**. Let's look at the full story of both.\"",
            "bodyHinglish": "Mr. Dabholkar apni bhanji Vaishnavi ke saath ghar ke bathroom mein khade the. Shelf par toilet cleaner ki ek bottle rakhi thi. Vaishnavi ne dekha ki label par do nishaan bane hain: ek khopdi-haddi ka, aur ek aisa jisme haath aur dhaatu par acid ki boondein girti dikhti hain. Neeche chhote akshar mein likha tha: \"sirf bade\".\n\n\"Mama, ye nishaan kya kehte hain?\" Mr. Dabholkar ne bottle ko shelf se uthaye bina label padha. \"Pehla nishaan: zehreela ya bahut hanikarak. Doosra: **corrosive**, yaani chamdi, aankh aur dhaatu ko jalane wala. Aur likha hai: 'bachchon se door rakhein', 'kisi aur safai wale ya bleach ke saath kabhi na milayein'.\" \"Aur andar kya hai?\" \"Label par ek acid ka naam hai: **hydrochloric acid**. Is bottle ko hum nahi kholenge, aur tum bhi kabhi nahi khologi.\"\n\nVaishnavi thodi der chup rahi, phir boli, \"Mama, par school mein padha tha ki hamare pet mein bhi hydrochloric acid hota hai. Jo toilet saaf karta hai, wahi mere andar? Phir mera pet kyun nahi jalta?\" Mr. Dabholkar muskuraye. \"Bahut achha sawaal. Jawab ke kuch hisse hain: bottle ka acid pet ke acid se kai guna **gaadha** hota hai, aur pet ki deewar par ek chikni parat hoti hai jo use bachati hai. Par ek aur baat hai: jise hum 'HCl' kehte hain wo ek **gas** bhi hai aur ek **ghol** bhi. Chalo, aaj dono ki poori kahani dekhte hain.\""
