            "heading": "Safety First",
            "headingHinglish": "Suraksha (pehle padho)",
            "body": "- **HCl gas** severely irritates the throat, nose, and eyes, and causes choking. The white \"fumes\" rising from concentrated hydrochloric acid contain this same gas.\n- **Concentrated H₂SO₄** (used to generate HCl in the lab) is intensely corrosive and destroys skin, fabric, and paper.\n- All of these procedures are carried out **in a school lab by a trained teacher inside a fume cupboard, wearing safety goggles and gloves**. Every preparation and demonstration in this topic is **for reading only or for observation as a teacher demo**. No student ever prepares, sniffs, or touches these chemicals.\n- **Never mix toilet cleaner or any acidic cleaner with bleach**: doing so releases deadly chlorine gas. Only adults should handle such bottles.\n- If any acid or gas ever contacts skin or eyes, inform a teacher or adult immediately. Do not attempt self-treatment—seek medical attention right away.",
