            "heading": "Introduction",
            "headingHinglish": "Introduction",
            "body": "In Topic 1, we saw HCl gas prepared from NaCl and concentrated H₂SO₄, and in Topic 2 we met ammonia, manufactured on a massive scale by the Haber process. One line in Topic 2's list of uses stood out: ammonia is also used to make **nitric acid**. Today we explore the full story of nitric acid—how it is prepared in the laboratory, how industry converts ammonia into nitric acid via the Ostwald process, why it behaves so differently from other acids when it meets metals, and how a famous two-acid partnership can dissolve even solid gold.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Topic 1 mein humne HCl gas ko NaCl aur concentrated H₂SO₄ se bante dekha, aur Topic 2 mein ammonia ko, jo Haber process se kaarkhaanon mein banti hai. Topic 2 ke uses mein ek line thi: ammonia se **nitric acid** bhi banta hai. Aaj usi acid ki kahani hai: wo lab mein kaise banta hai, kaarkhaane mein ammonia se kaise banta hai (Ostwald process), wo dhatuon ke saath \"ulta\" kyun chalta hai, aur wo kaun sa jodi hai jo gold ko bhi gala deta hai."
