            "heading": "Chapter Summary",
            "headingHinglish": "Chapter ka saar",
            "body": "| Topic | Core Focus | One-Line Takeaway |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | HCl gas and hydrochloric acid | Prepared from NaCl + conc. H₂SO₄ and collected by upward displacement; dry HCl is covalent, becoming an acid only in water |\n| 2 | Ammonia: from lab to farm | Prepared from NH₄Cl + Ca(OH)₂, dried over CaO, collected by downward displacement; made industrially via the Haber process for fertilisers |\n| 3 | Nitric acid | Prepared from KNO₃ + conc. H₂SO₄ in all-glass apparatus; made via the Ostwald process; strong oxidiser that yields NO/NO₂ (not H₂) and forms aqua regia with HCl |\n| 4 | Sulphuric acid: Contact process | S → SO₂ → SO₃ (over V₂O₅ at ~450 °C) → oleum (H₂S₂O₇) → H₂SO₄; never bubble SO₃ straight into water |\n| 5 | Concentrated H₂SO₄ | Acts as a dehydrating agent, hot oxidising agent, non-volatile acid, and drying agent; always add Acid to Water, never the reverse |\n| 6 | Putting it all together | Use solubility, vapour density, and acid-base/redox nature to choose collection and drying methods and identify unknown compounds |\n\nYou now know all four industrial giants of inorganic chemistry—an acid gas, a basic gas, a powerful oxidising acid, and the king of dehydrating acids. Fantastic work!\n\n**What's next?** In Chapter 10, **Carbon and Its Compounds**, we turn to a single element that forms millions of compounds—from sugar, soap, and fabrics to fuels and plastics: **carbon**. Why is carbon so uniquely versatile? Let's find out!",
            "bodyHinglish": "| Topic | Kya seekha | Ek line |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | HCl gas aur hydrochloric acid | NaCl aur conc. H₂SO₄ se banti hai, upward displacement; dry HCl gas khud acidic nahi, paani se acid |\n| 2 | Ammonia: lab se khet tak | NH₄Cl aur Ca(OH)₂ se, downward displacement, CaO se sukhti; Haber se khaad |\n| 3 | Nitric acid | KNO₃ aur conc. H₂SO₄ se; Ostwald; oxidiser, H₂ nahi; aqua regia |\n| 4 | Sulphuric acid: Contact process | S se SO₂, SO₃ (V₂O₅), oleum, phir H₂SO₄; SO₃ seedha paani mein nahi |\n| 5 | Concentrated H₂SO₄ | Dehydrator, oxidiser, drying agent; acid ko paani mein, ulta kabhi nahi |\n| 6 | Sab kuch mila kar | Gas jama karna aur sukhana; clue se pehchaan; catalyst sirf raftaar |\n\nChaaron kirdaar ab tumhari pehchaan mein hain: ek acid, ek base-wali gas, ek oxidiser, aur ek dehydrator. Shabaash!\n\nAage kya? Chapter 10 Carbon and Its Compounds mein: cheeni, sabun, plastic aur petrol ke peeche ek hi tatva hai, carbon: wo itne lakhon compounds kyun banata hai?"
