            "correctIndex": 3,
            "explanation": "Pitfall to avoid (\"Carbon compounds are ionic because sodium ethanoate and soap contain metal ions.\"): *Correction:* Carbon never forms simple ionic $\\text{C}^{4+}$ or $\\text{C}^{4-}$ ions because the energy required to transfer 4 electrons is prohibitively large. The carbon skeleton in organic molecules is held together strictly by covalent bonds! In sodium ethanoate ($\\text{CH}_3\\text{COO}^-\\text{Na}^+$) and soap ($\\text{C}_{17}\\text{H}_{35}\\text{COO}^-\\text{Na}^+$), the carbon-carbon, carbon-hydrogen, and carbon-oxygen bonds are all robust covalent bonds. The ionic attraction exists purely between the terminal oxygen anion ($\\text{O}^-$) and the external sodium cation ($\\text{Na}^+$).",
            "explanationHinglish": "Bachke rehna (\"Carbon ke compound ionic hote hain: carbon bhi sodium ki tarah electron deta ya leta hai.\"): Topic 1 mein dekha tha ki carbon C⁴⁺ ya C⁴⁻ nahi banata, wo covalent bond banata hai. To phir sodium ethanoate (Topic 7) aur sabun (Topic 8) ionic kaise? Maan lo teacher ne pencil-LED jaisa 2 cell ka tester ([chemical-bonding-part4.md](../../../class9/chemistry/chemical-bonding/chemical-bonding-part4.md)) lagakar paanch ghol jaanche (sirf dekhne ke liye): | Ghol | LED | Kyun | |---|---|---| | ethanol paani mein | nahi jalti | covalent, ion nahi | | glucose paani mein | nahi jalti | covalent, ion nahi | | halka ethanoic acid | dheemi jalti hai | thode hi molecule ion banate hain (weak acid) | | sodium ethanoate paani mein | tez jalti hai | Na⁺ aur CH₃COO⁻ ion | | sabun (sodium stearate) paani mein | jalti hai | Na⁺ aur C₁₇H₃₅COO⁻ ion | Dhyan se dekho: charge carbon par nahi, oxygen par hai. CH₃COO⁻ ke andar C–C, C–H aur C–O bond sab covalent hain; ionic jod sirf Na⁺ aur O⁻ ke beech hai. Niyam: carbon apne saathi atoms ke saath hamesha covalent bond banata hai. Kisi organic namak mein ionic bond bhi ho sakta hai, par wo carbon ke electron dene-lene se nahi."
