            "correctIndex": 0,
            "explanation": "Pitfall to avoid (\"Carbon monoxide (CO) and carbon dioxide (CO₂) are virtually identical gases.\"): *Correction:* A difference of a single oxygen atom completely changes their chemical identity, physical properties, and physiological impacts: - CO₂ (Carbon Dioxide): Molar mass 44 g/mol; non-toxic; non-combustible; turns limewater milky; greenhouse gas essential for plant photosynthesis. - CO (Carbon Monoxide): Molar mass 28 g/mol; highly flammable (burns with a blue flame); does not turn limewater milky; a silent, lethal poison that binds irreversibly to blood haemoglobin, causing fatal asphyxiation.",
            "explanationHinglish": "Bachke rehna (\"CO aur CO₂ ek jaisi gas hain: bas ek oxygen ka farak hai.\"): Ek atom ka farak bhi bahut bada ho sakta hai. Dono ko 11.2 L (STP) lo: ye 0.5 mol hai. CO ka mass 0.5 × 28 = 14 g, CO₂ ka 0.5 × 44 = 22 g. | Gun | CO | CO₂ | |---|---|---| | Molar mass | 28 | 44 | | Lime water | koi badlaav nahi | doodhiya | | Jalna | khud jalti hai (neeli lau) | jalti nahi, aag bujhane mein kaam aati hai | | Gandh aur asar | bina rang, bina gandh, zehreeli | bina rang, bina gandh, zehreeli nahi (par bahut zyada ho to saans ke liye oxygen kam) | | Kahan banti hai | adhoora jalne se (Topic 1 aur 4) | poora jalne se, saans, fermentation | Niyam: formula ke ek atom ka farak poora swabhaav badal deta hai. Band kamre mein koyla jalne par CO banti hai, jo jaan le sakti hai; CO₂ se wo khatra nahi (par hawadaar kamra phir bhi zaroori)."
